title An alias needs an owner
prompt the standing baton -- take the next agent-doable lap in the language lane
think Cold roster open first, held still while it ran: 232 green, 2 red, 2 gated (%5), tree_moved=no. Both reds predate me -- tame_reach 553 against a ceiling of 552, raised when tools/rye/wrap_ring.rye landed uncovered in 44526f250, and standing_equipment red behind it. Three ships had already named tame_reach as a peer's lane; seed_link had gone green since my last lap.
think The lap before this one built glow_shared_bound, which gates a bound published by two Glow modules at zero divergence, and left a question on the card: tokens.rye imports nothing, so one module could own max_name_len and thirteen could alias it. This lap took that door.
think Read the fourteen declarations up close before touching one, which is the water row's whole instruction. Every rune head bounds a face or an arm name, every one of those is an ident, and the lexer is what decides where an ident ends. So the owner is glow/tokens.rye and the law is the language's rather than any module's -- one name length, or the lexer accepts a name a parser refuses.
think The other six shared names are pairs of PEERS -- max_test_len in rune_assert and rune_conditional, max_subject_len in rune_null and rune_switch, max_stem_len, lent_demo_len, two gth_ ticks. Neither member owns the name, so an alias would invent an arbitrary dependency between equals. That is why this stopped at one name of seven, and it is the lap's finding: an alias needs an owner, and where there is none the wall is the mechanism.
think Applying the change reddened my own guard, one day old. Its last leg asserted the census still printed `name agreed max_name_len` -- a specimen, pinned one line beneath its own comment warning that an expected value pinned in a second place is a stale pin waiting for a tree that moved. It moved the same day. The repair moved the canary into the instrument: the scan refuses a population of zero declarations, since a pattern that has stopped matching prints exactly what a clean tree prints, and the witness leg now asks only that some name is still shared.
obs Mechanism: glow/tokens.rye keeps `pub const max_name_len: u32 = 64;` with a rewritten doc comment naming why it owns the number; thirteen modules -- expr.rye, rune_shape.rye and eleven rune heads -- read `pub const max_name_len: u32 = tokens.max_name_len;`, twelve of them gaining `const tokens = @import("tokens.rye");` (rune_shape already imported it). tokens.rye imports only std, so no cycle is possible. rune_core.rye's invariant comment about rune_face's copy "happening to be 64 here too" now says the two are one declaration.
obs The census fell rather than rose: shared_names 7 -> 6, declarations 197 -> 184, files_read 134. An alias publishes no number, so it leaves the wall entirely -- which is the shape a repair should have.
obs Not idempotent, and I caught it by running it twice: my scratch awk aliases the OWNER to itself if handed tokens.rye. Its safety lived in my hand rather than in the tool. The tool was scratch under .lap/ and dies with the lap; the fault is named here rather than left implied.
obs Graded what I touched: glow/tokens.rye A 93, glow/rune_core.rye A 95, the scan B+ 85, the witness C+ 79 -- one frame, worked down in place. Its module head read 55 percent negative sentences; rewritten holding every claim, path and number exactly, it reads 33 percent and B 84.
loom witness=glow_shared_bound legs=32 shared_names=6 declarations=184 files_read=134
loom roster=cold guards_green=232 guards_red=2 guards_gated=2 guards_cpu_ms=2503754
rota lap 4558, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; its cardinal seat asks a lap to RUN the census rather than quote it, and tools/c/convergence_census.sh reads 12 candidates, 10 proven, 2 unproven. The seat's own page records that same number falling fourfold and rising again as the instrument learned to find evidence by more than a filename stem.
file glow/tokens.rye the owner: the literal 64, and a comment saying why the lexer holds it
file glow/rune_core.rye the alias, plus the invariant comment that had described two numbers agreeing
file tools/fixtures/g/glow_shared_bound_scan.sh refuses a zero-declaration population; header tells the new truth
file tools/fixtures/g/glow_shared_bound_control.sh leg 16, the refusal planted and lifted, 30 -> 32
file tools/g/glow_shared_bound_witness.rish the specimen canary retired for a structural one
file construction/ITINERARY.md the account, elder shelved whole at 20260910.092558
scope one keystone -- one shared Glow bound given one owner, thirteen aliases, and the guard restated
status GREEN -- 20 Glow witnesses on metal (11 rune heads, expr, face_lit, four lower hops, shop-nest parse, rune alphabet), glow_shared_bound, glow_literal_law, glow_decimal_law, glow_desk_reach, ascii_comment, tame_style_check, width-check, and three real desks lowered and built through glow_run. Hot close pending in this same send.
recommend keep-going -- the six peer pairs stand walled and answered; the next language lap is whether a peer pair ever earns an owner, which is Keaton's word rather than mine
